PATCH 309: reconstruct FUN_0000_0459 = the 3-in/3-out fixed-point ROTATION TRIG the per-frame camera
feed (FUN_1000_a20d -> a192 -> 0459) uses to rotate the view-offset deltas by the vehicle heading, and
wire its faithful multi-return into a20d.  asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin 0x459-0x4c7
(DS=SS=DGROUP=0x1c00).

0459 is a STACK-FRAME function (asm 0x459 `mov bp,sp`; four PUSHes build the locals [bp-2..bp-8]).
Ghidra could not resolve the SS stack base in the __allregs flat model -> it emitted the unbound global
`register0x00000010` for every [bp-N] access (a deref of host address -6/-8 => SIGSEGV the instant the
function is executed), AND -- because a192 is a bare far thunk (`call 0x459; lret`) that Ghidra typed
2-arg -- it DROPPED the cx (heading) register INPUT and the dx/cx register OUTPUTS (the `extraout_`
multi-return class).  Inputs: ax=param_1 (angle A), dx=param_2 (magnitude M, 0xaaa), cx=heading H.
Trig helpers: FUN_0000_05e2 = signed fixed-point SIN core (magnitude in ax; CF -- "value==1.0, skip the
mul" -- signalled by the sole reachable return 0xffff, asm je 0x632 / CARRY2 -> return -1,stc);
FUN_0000_05dd(x) = 05e2(0x4000-x) = COS.  The sine SIGN is the input angle's bit15 (asm `cwd` at 0x5e2
entry, BEFORE the C wrapper's 0x7fff mask); for 05dd the cwd sees the pre-folded (0x4000-x).  Outputs
(asm 0x4c1/0x4c3/0x4c4 `mov ax,dx; pop dx; pop cx`): ax = block-4 5dd(L2); dx = block-3 5e2(L2);
cx = block-1 5e2(H), where L2 = 0x4000-A.

Reconstructed with real C locals (the [bp-N] frame) + the cx input threaded from the shim global
g_fist_rot_h (set by a20d, the immediate synchronous caller) + the dx/cx outputs published into
g_fist_rot_dx/g_fist_rot_cx.  FUN_1000_a20d now sets g_fist_rot_h = the vehicle heading word[di+0x38]
(asm 0x1a232) and uses 0459's rotated dx/cx returns for the 0x9618/0x961c camera deltas -- resolving the
patch-308 documented `dx=0xaaa` camera-fidelity residual.  The object-projection a192 callers
(FUN_1000_addb / fist.c 60861/60907, the DORMANT per-object path) don't set g_fist_rot_h and ignore the
dx/cx outputs, so they are unchanged (non-crashing; heading imprecise-as-before, same dropped-cx class).

MISSION-PATH ONLY (a20d runs only inside the d548/d549-gated op-0x24 poster 795c) + a latent-crash
removal (register0x00000010 -> a real frame) -> strictly behaviour-neutral for the 19 menu/pre-mission
verify flows (verify.sh both = 19/19).  Shim globals in tools/native_main.c.

